      "documentConcept": "Impulse control disorders and dopamine dysregulation",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:437bab553503b91e212b865d84e317d64e393ce0cd6faf1acdb9cf1ee5bb5fe0",
      "text": "Impulse control disorders in Parkinson\u2019s disease include harmful gambling, shopping, sexual behaviour and binge eating. Dopamine dysregulation syndrome involves compulsive medication overuse; punding involves repetitive, purposeless activity. Dopamine agonists carry a major ICD risk, although other dopaminergic therapy can also be implicated. Prevention requires candid patient and family counselling and repeated behavioural review. Management generally starts with specialist-guided gradual agonist reduction, while watching motor control and withdrawal. DDS can require a different medication-reduction strategy. Specialist cognitive behavioural therapy may help persistent ICDs, but trial limitations and endpoint-dependent drug results argue against overstating treatment certainty.",
